is a process based credential cache.  To use it, set the environ‐
ment variable to or add the stanza

[libdefaults]
        default_cc_name = KCM:%{uid}

to  the configuration file and make sure is started in the system
startup files.  The daemon can hold the credentials for all users
in the system.  Access control is  done  with  Unix‐like  permis‐
sions.   The  daemon checks the access on all operations based on
the uid and gid of the user.  The tickets are renewed as long  as
is  permitted  by  the  KDC’s policy.  The daemon can also keep a
SYSTEM credential that server processes can use  to  access  ser‐
vices.   One  example  of  usage might be an nss_ldap module that
quickly needs to get credentials and doesn’t want  to  renew  the
ticket  itself.  Supported options: system cache name location of
config file system cache group max size for a kcm‐request  disal‐
low  extracting  any krbtgt from the daemon.  detach from console
